# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Before this, the repo held a mix: 26 files committed with CRLF (the original
# codebase) and 11 with LF (later additions). With no rule in place, any tool
# that rewrote a file wholesale flipped its endings, and Git then reported every
# line as changed — a three-line README edit once produced a 293-line diff.
#
# text=auto  — Git decides text vs binary per file
# eol=lf     — text files are LF in the index AND checked out as LF everywhere,
#              so Windows contributors cannot reintroduce CRLF by editing.
* text=auto eol=lf
